Z||000000||Stan86SE||04-16-2001||05:47 PM||||I'm putting a new pickup coil on (which has been no problem), but I need to know just exactly where the new O ring goes.  I know that sounds completely ridiculous, but the old O ring is nowhere to be found on the distributor, so I have nothing to go by.  Can somebody tell me, please, as I'd like to get the distributor back in the car before I run out of daylight today (soon).  Many thanks!<P>- Stan <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Stan86SE||04-16-2001||05:56 PM||||Common sense tells me that the O ring should go all the way up to the top where the distributor base mates with the block, but the O ring would have to be stretched to do that...???  Anybody?<P>- Stan||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||04-16-2001||06:19 PM||||Stan, it should be stretched a little, so it seats in its groove and seals tight.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Stan86SE||04-16-2001||08:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85Josh:<BR><B>Stan, it should be stretched a little, so it seats in its groove and seals tight.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks, Josh.  (How's it goin', BTW?)  The replacement O ring I had seemed to be too small to me at first just by looking at it, and I was a little worried about trying to "force" it on.  As it turns out, it went on just fine.  Thanks again for the reply.  I believe I've met my quota for stupid questions today! ;-)<P>- Stan||||reg||1
Z||000004||85Josh||04-16-2001||09:55 PM||||I think the only stupid questions are the ones you don't ask! Or at least, the ones that you can't find in a search! I'm doing great, looking forward to heading down to Alabama next weekend. I'm gonna be in uniform(National Guard) this weekend, doing traffic/crowd control for Thunder over Louisville.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Stan86SE||04-16-2001||10:04 PM||||Glad you're doing well, Josh!  Hope your Fiero's running smooth, too.  It'll probably be a madhouse at Thunder.  I doubt that I'll fight the crowd and traffic.  If the weather holds, it should be a great show though, as usual.  Take it easy!<P>- Stan||||reg||12
